course: dictionary
lesson: 15035
title: Starting again: the word resumption
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Resumption is a formal word for starting something again after it has stopped. It comes from the verb resume, which means to begin again. Think of a paused film: when you press play, the film resumes.
explain: «After the storm, the resumption of train services began at noon.» The trains had stopped, and now they start again. The clue words are «after the storm» and «began», so resumption must mean the restart.
explain: You will often see resumption in news, notices and sport. «The referee blew the whistle for the resumption of play.» Everyday words for the same idea are restart and start again, so «the restart of play» means nearly the same, but resumption sounds more formal.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «After the storm, the restart of train services began at noon» still makes sense, so restart is a good everyday swap. Use this swap test every time you meet a hard word.
fact: Resumption is a noun, and it is usually singular: the resumption of talks.
fact: «Resumption» means starting something again after it has stopped.
fact: «Resumption» can also mean the return of something that had paused, such as lessons after a holiday.
fact: Everyday words for resumption are restart and start again.
fact: Common phrases with resumption are: resumption of play, resumption of talks, and resumption of school.
exercise: «The team waited ten minutes, then the resumption of the match began.» What does resumption mean here? | A new match with new players | *The match starting again after a break | The end of the match | The match being cancelled for ever
exercise: Maria says resumption is just a fancy word for restart. Is she right? | No, it means a holiday | No, it means a loud noise | *Yes, it is close to restart, because both mean starting again | No, it means stopping
exercise: The school announced the ___ of lessons on Monday. Which word fits best? | ending | *resumption | silence | breakfast
test: «The news said the resumption of peace talks would be on Friday.» What does resumption mean? | A long journey | *Starting again after a stop | Stopping for good | A quiet break
test: Which everyday word is closest in meaning to resumption? | Silence | *Restart | Ending | Pause
exam: Read «Play stopped for the rain, and the resumption came after lunch.» What does resumption mean, and which everyday word could replace it? | Stopping, so end | *Starting again, so restart | Raining, because of the wet grass | Eating, because of lunch
